 "verdict": "**B — THERE IS NO BREAK, and this is the outcome I would least like.**\n  Observed Δmax **0.359**; a series with **no break at all**, carrying the real marginal collapse, returns a median of **0.230** and a 95th percentile of **0.386**.\n  ⇒ **`#886`①'s two-eras sentence is WITHDRAWN.** The `+0.340` / `−0.373` flip between all-waves and 1990+ is what cutting 28 noisy points in two produces for free, and I wrote a design brief on it. **The closing sentence of a round is a claim, and that one had no control until now.**\n  ⚠⚠ **And the specification curve is where the honesty is.** The piecewise-LINEAR cell reads Δmax 0.552 — which clears the MEAN model's null and would have been a finding — but judged against **its own** null (0.690, larger because it fits 4 parameters to 2) it is INSIDE. Across the 48-cell grid, **8 cells clear their own model's null and they place the break at 9 DIFFERENT YEARS** — pick a specification and you can date a regime change anywhere from 1977 to 2012.\n  ⚠⚠ **And the location bootstrap is the trap this round exists to name**: **93.8% of bootstrap breakpoints fall in 1977–1985**, which reads as a confident date — **for a break that is not there**. A location estimate is CONDITIONAL on the feature existing; its tightness is never evidence that it does.\n  ⚠ And a null here is a **bound**: 28 irregular points have low power against anything but a large regime change, so this says *no break large enough for this design to see*, never *the coupling was continuous*.",
 "gate_ok": false
}